--[[
    Quartz Scanner - Anomaly Artefact Scanner

    Placement:
    - The device is placed through the Hideout Furniture placement system
      (functor wiring in items_zad_devices.ltx).
    - Placement is only allowed inside a major anomaly field, identified with:
      known anomaly-field story objects (the addon's STATIC_FIELD_SPOTS list),
      DAO smart spots (smart_map_for_DAO.dao_spots) and smarts showing a
      field circle on the map.
    - Three enforcement layers: the check runs when the player starts placing
      (func_place_item), when the device is confirmed (wrapped
      placeable_furniture.createObject) and one update after the device was
      created (post-placement check in quartz_device.init). The last layer
      does not depend on Hideout Furniture internals, so moving out of the
      field with the device in placement mode can never keep a placement.
    - If placement is attempted outside a field it is cancelled, the device
      is refunded and st_zad_quartz_placement_impossible is shown.
    - When a placement succeeds, a news tip announces the field the device
      is surveying: st_zad_quartz_surveying
      ("QUARTZ-1M is now surveying <zone> in <location>").
    - When the device is picked up again, a news tip announces that it
      stopped surveying: st_zad_quartz_stopped_surveying
      ("QUARTZ-1M is no longer surveying <zone> in <location>").
    - The surveyed field (smart or named spot) is registered in the device's
      own state (hf_obj_manager) when it is placed and unregistered when it
      is picked up, so the field name and identity are always available.
    - A global survey driver watches the registered fields. Checks are
      event-driven instead of continuous: one fires after a save load, when
      the player enters a different anomaly zone, and as in-game time
      passes - which covers sleeping, time skips, guides and fast travel.
      Fields are only checked while the player is on their level, because
      the artefact spawner only fills the anomaly zones of the loaded
      level. When a check finds new artefacts, one combined tip is sent
      with a bullet point per anomaly zone covered by a Quartz device
      (st_zad_quartz_artefacts_detected / st_zad_quartz_artefacts_line):
      "New artefacts detected in <level>:\n- <zone>: <artefact>, <artefact>"
      The registry of surveyed devices is saved with the game, and placed
      devices are re-registered by the scan itself when found; entries are
      only removed when the device is picked up.
      The first check after placement only establishes a baseline, so
      artefacts already lying in the field are not announced.

    The placed object is bound through quartz_device.init.
]]

-- Sections (must match items_zad_devices.ltx)
local QUARTZ_ITEM_SECTION      = "zad_device_quartz"
local QUARTZ_PLACEABLE_SECTION = "placeable_zad_device_quartz"

-- Major anomaly field identification.
--
-- Fields are located through
--   1. the known anomaly-field story objects (the addon's STATIC_FIELD_SPOTS
--      list, duplicated here since pda.script keeps its table script-local)
--   2. anomaly spots of the "Smart Dynamic Anomalies" module
--      (smart_map_for_DAO.dao_spots, resolved through SIMBOARD.smarts_by_names)
--   3. any smart terrain that currently shows a field circle on the map
--      (the white primary_object spot)
-- A position counts as inside a field when it lies within FIELD_MATCH_RADIUS
-- metres of one of those field centres (2D distance).
local FIELD_MATCH_RADIUS = 15
local FREE_PARENT_ID     = 65535
local NORMAL_SPOT        = "primary_object"

-- Artefact detection by surveying devices. The scan runs from a global
-- driver (not from the device wrapper), so it keeps working while a device
-- is offline (player far away but on the same level).
--
-- There is no continuous sweep: a survey check is fired by events - a save
-- load, the player entering an anomaly zone, and in-game time passing
-- (sleep, time skips, guides and fast travel all advance the game clock).
-- Fields are only checked while the player is on their level, because the
-- artefact spawner only fills the anomaly zones of the loaded level
-- (grok_artefacts_random_spawner / bind_anomaly_zone iterate the current
-- level's zones)
local ARTEFACT_SCAN_RADIUS  = 50    -- metres around the field centre
local ARTEFACT_SCAN_CHUNK   = 300   -- alife object ids processed per update
local SURVEY_CHECK_DELAY    = 1000  -- milliseconds between an event and its sweep
local SURVEY_CHECK_INTERVAL = 300   -- game seconds between time-based checks
local ZONE_POLL_INTERVAL    = 5     -- seconds between anomaly-zone polls

